    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43512" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēmĭnālis</span></b> ,
		e, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj</i> [semen], <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to seed</i>, <i>good for seed</i>, <i>seminal</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vicia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					11, 2, 76</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">membrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Auct. Priap. 26, 2</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">venae, Lact. Opif. Dei, 12: viae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Acut. 3, 18, 180</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vascula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Theod. Prisc. 4, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vita,</span>”
				<i>vegetable</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Mam. Stat. Anim. 1, 21</span></i>
			.—<i>Plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sē-mĭnālia</span></b> ,
			n., <i>standing crops</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 13 <i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
